### Screens Completed

1. **Laboratory Entry (`ui/LabEditor.kt`, clinical lab panels)**
   - **Option A: One list, type in place** — Panel selection (First Trimester Booking, Preeclampsia Workup, GDM, Anemia, Infection) adds all constituent tests in a single tap; batch date and lab set once at top; in-row typing for numbers and inline chips for serology; automated reference range flags (`Normal ✓`, `High ▲`, `Low ▼`) with 1-tap popover override; single-test search; zero separate Normal/Abnormal switches; zero mentions of the word "Codex".
   - **Option B: One test at a time, number keypad** — Dedicated on-screen keypad to eliminate keyboard jump and layout shifts; auto-advances through the panel upon entry; review tab showing the complete batch overview.

2. **Ultrasound Entry (`ui/UltrasoundEditor.kt`)**
   - **Option A: Picture cards and steppers** — Graphical anatomical choice cards for placenta site (anterior, posterior, fundal, lateral, low-lying, previa), amniotic fluid/liquor, fetal presentation, and fetal number; smart biometry steppers (FHR, BPD, HC, AC, FL, EFW) pre-calibrated to 28w GA typical medians; dating calculation hint area with redating threshold advice; "✨ From my choices" automated clinical impression synthesizer; collapsible photo attachments and linked visit selector.
   - **Option B: Start from a normal scan, one finding at a time** — 1-tap "Fill normal scan" button; live updating single-line report string; auto-advancing accordion rows; biometry sliders with fine-step adjusters.

3. **Medication Entry (`ui/MedicationEditor.kt`)**
   - **Option A: Build one prescription card** — Pick from common antenatal drugs or recent patient medications; pre-fills standard obstetric dose, route, and frequency; 1-tap chips for frequency and route; start date defaults to today; prophylaxis indicator badge; active medication list below with 1-tap stop (completed vs discontinued) and inline edit; 5-second undo toast.
   - **Option B: One tap to add, fix it in the list** — Instant-add from drug catalog; newly added drug highlighted with interactive tokens directly on the row to tweak dose or frequency without opening a separate editing form; inline stop and edit actions.

